1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,369
You're probably an idiot if you buy coffee every single day.

2
00:00:03,569 --> 00:00:04,504
Here's the math.

3
00:00:04,904 --> 00:00:09,213
Six dollars a day. That's two thousand one hundred ninety dollars a year.

4
00:00:09,513 --> 00:00:16,162
What if you invested it instead? Assume a seven percent average yearly return. An assumption, not a promise.

5
00:00:16,462 --> 00:00:18,765
Hit like if you're holding a coffee right now.

6
00:00:19,066 --> 00:00:21,943
After ten years: about thirty thousand dollars.

7
00:00:22,243 --> 00:00:24,280
Twenty years: about ninety thousand.

8
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:27,407
Send this to the friend with a latte in their hand.

9
00:00:27,707 --> 00:00:30,525
Thirty years: about two hundred seven thousand.

10
00:00:30,825 --> 00:00:33,731
Follow along, because the last ten years are insane.

11
00:00:34,081 --> 00:00:37,866
Forty years: about four hundred thirty-seven thousand dollars.

12
00:00:38,266 --> 00:00:39,069
For coffee.

13
00:00:39,569 --> 00:00:40,854
STILL WANT THAT LATTE?
